  {
    "text": "Kessipramol is a strong inhibitor of HTX-5D, and Sevipramol requires HTX-5D to form its active metabolite. Taking them together would be expected to reduce formation of Sevipramol’s active metabolite, potentially lowering its pharmacological activity. Because a strong inhibitor affects a required activation pathway for Sevipramol, this is a clinically significant pharmacokinetic interaction.\n\nMECHANISM: Kessipramol inhibits HTX-5D, decreasing Sevipramol active metabolite formation\nFINAL ANSWER: YES",
